===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|defeten}}, from {{der|en|enm|defet|t=disfigured|pos=past participle}} and {{m|enm|defet|t=defect|pos=noun}}, see Etymology 2 below.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[overcome]] in [[battle]] or [[contest]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:defeat}}
#: {{ux|en|Wellington '''defeated''' Napoleon at Waterloo.}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1917
|author=Samuel Couling
|chapter=Japanese Relations with China
|title=The Encyclopaedia Sinica
|url=https://archive.org/details/encyclopaediasi00coul/
|year_published=1964
|publisher=Literature House, Ltd.
|OCLC=9990545
|page=255
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/encyclopaediasi00coul/page/255/
|column=2
|text=The Japanese '''defeated''' the Ming general Tsu Chʻeng-hsün {{lang|zh|祖承訓}} at Pʻing jang {{lang|ko|平壤}} in 1592, the first year of Bunroku {{lang|zh|文祿}} of Japan, and the fighting continued for some years; but at Hideyoshi's death the Japanese troops left Korea.}}
#* {{quote-web
|en
|date=August 01, 1980
|origdate=1 May 1980
|author=[[w:Chiang Ching-kuo|Ching-kuo Chiang]]
|title=President Chiang Ching-kuo continues his period of mourning and finds that visits to countryside and people give him renewed strength
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20200517074534/https://taiwantoday.tw/print.php?unit=4&post=5149
|archivedate=17 May 2020
|work=w:Taiwan Today
|text=My personal success or failure is insignificant; the rise or fall of the nation is my responsibility and must not be shirked. Upon introspection, I feel I am firmer than ever in confidence that the Communists will be '''defeated'''. These are feelings which will comfort Father's soul in Heaven.}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Arlette Saenz|title=James Talarico defeats Jasmine Crockett to win Democratic primary in Texas Senate race|url=https://www.cnn.com/2026/03/04/politics/james-talarico-texas-senate-primary|date=2026-03-04|passage=The 36-year-old '''defeats''' US Rep. Jasmine Crockett, a fiery 44-year-old Democrat from the Dallas area, in a contentious primary that became increasingly personal.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260308211757/https://www.cnn.com/2026/03/04/politics/james-talarico-texas-senate-primary}}
